<EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>
You use antislop (Anti Slop: Rules for AI Coding Agents), installed from https://github.com/miqdadbadjuber/anti-slop (v3.2.25). It is a filter, not a style guide: it stops generic AI slop in generated UI, copy, and code, without prescribing aesthetics.

For UI, copy, people, mobile layout, or code comments work, read the installed skill files directly:
- Core filter, always on: `.cursor/skills/antislop/SKILL.md`
- UI / visual: `.cursor/skills/antislop-ui/SKILL.md`
- Copy & text: `.cursor/skills/antislop-copywriting/SKILL.md`
- People: `.cursor/skills/antislop-human/SKILL.md`
- Mobile / responsive: `.cursor/skills/antislop-layoutmobile/SKILL.md`
- Code comments: `.cursor/skills/antislop-code/SKILL.md`
Before starting, follow the core's "Two Usage Modes" section: explicit session instruction first, then global preference, then ask. For a resolved mode, announce `antislop active: <mode> (session override).` or `antislop active: <mode> (global preference).` once, using the actual mode and source. Ask only when no mode is resolved.

Read `DESIGN.md` for this site's identity before changing the look. The filter sits on top of that direction.
</EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>
